B.G5=new A.rN("01","Missing MFA","MFA",B.F7,"Initial access","One stolen password was all it took.","Attackers signed in to a remote-access portal with stolen credentials. The portal asked for a password, but nothing else.","The remote-access portal only required a username and password.","A password stolen through phishing or reuse was enough to let an outsider into the network.","Require multi-factor authentication, ideally a phishing-resistant security key rather than a code that can be intercepted.")
B.F5=new A.ee(63169,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.G4=new A.rN("02","Outdated Systems","Updates",B.F5,"Known exploits","Old servers kept known flaws alive.","Once inside, the attackers found systems that had missed updates. Known flaws in that old software gave them a firmer foothold.","Old, unsupported software may stop receiving security updates.","Attackers could exploit published vulnerabilities that already had fixes available.","Test and install updates on a regular schedule, and replace systems that can no longer receive patches.")
B.F8=new A.ee(983861,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.G3=new A.rN("03","Poor Network Separation","Network",B.F8,"Lateral movement","A flat network let the breach spread.","Because the internal network was largely flat, the attackers could move from one system to another without meeting a real boundary.","Unnecessary connections can let an attacker reach other systems.","One infected device could lead to a much wider outage.","Separate important systems from each other and allow only the connections each one actually needs.")
